Golden Sun Recompiled for Android -- licence and credits
=========================================================

This app is an Android port of Golden Sun Recompiled. It contains no Golden Sun game data, ROM, BIOS,
music, art or code derived from the game: you supply your own legally obtained Golden Sun ROM (USA or
Europe), and the app translates and compiles the game code on your own device, into its private storage.
Nothing of the game is uploaded or bundled. Golden Sun belongs to Nintendo and Camelot Software Planning.

WHAT IS WHOSE

  Android port (the Android shell and glue, the settings and menus, the touch and gamepad controls, the
  GLES3 display layer, the Descore shell)
      Copyright (c) 2026 wootbeer   https://github.com/wootbeer
      Licensed under the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 (full text below).

  Golden Sun Recompiled (the Golden Sun layer: the game-specific translation data, runner and renderers)
      By Shmargus   https://github.com/Shmargus/GSRecomp
      Vendored here at version 0.3.1. Used under whatever terms its author provides; see that project's
      LICENSE and ATTRIBUTION.md.

  gbarecomp (the GBA emulation and recompilation engine)
      Copyright (c) 2026 Matthew Stan   https://github.com/mstan/gbarecomp
      Licensed under the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 (full text below, and in
      gsrandroid/src/main/cpp/gsrecomp/gbarecomp/LICENSE). Portions are derived from mGBA (MPL-2.0) and
      JRickey/gba-recomp (MIT OR Apache-2.0); see gsrandroid/src/main/cpp/gsrecomp/gbarecomp/
      THIRD_PARTY_ATTRIBUTION.md, which must stay with any copy of this project.

  TinyCC (the on-device C compiler)
      Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1; the full text is in
      gsrandroid/src/main/cpp/tcc/COPYING and its source is included in this project.
      gsrandroid/src/main/cpp/tcc/tccelf.c has been modified for this port.

  Screen filters (Display > Screen filter), as ported by Golden Sun Recompiled from libretro's glsl-shaders
      LCD3x by Gigaherz -- public domain.
      CRT Lottes by Timothy Lottes -- public domain.
      xBR-lv2, Copyright (C) 2011-2016 Hyllian -- MIT licence; the full notice is in
      licenses/xBR-lv2-MIT.txt and gsrandroid/src/main/cpp/gsr/gsr_screen_filter_shaders.inc, and is shown in
      the app's Credits screen.

THIS PROJECT IS NONCOMMERCIAL. The engine it cannot run without is licensed for noncommercial use only,
so this app may not be sold, and it carries no ads or paid features.

